  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "A random sample of $100$ students from a particular university yields a mean GPA of $3.1$ with a sample standard deviation of $0.48.$ Find a  $90%$ confidence interval for the population mean GPA $\\mu $ of all students.  \n\n*Hint: Given a random variable $T$ that has a student's $t$-distribution ${T}_{k}$ with $k$ degrees of freedom, the table below shows the $t$-scores ${t}_{k,p}$ such that $P(T>{t}_{k,p})=p$ for some particular values of $k$ and $p.$*\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $99$ | $\\,1.290\\,$ | $\\,1.660\\,$ | $\\,1.984\\,$ | $\\,2.365\\,$ | $\\,2.626\\,$ |\n| $100$ | $\\,1.290\\,$ | $\\,1.660\\,$ | $\\,1.984\\,$ | $\\,2.364\\,$ | $\\,2.626\\,$ |\n| $101$ | $\\,1.290\\,$ | $\\,1.660\\,$ | $\\,1.984\\,$ | $\\,2.364\\,$ | $\\,2.625\\,$ |",
